  "duration": 56.193,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.93,
      "text": "A cosmic structure ten billion light-years long shouldn't exist.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Three-dimensional distribution of dark matter in the Universe (artist's impression) (heic0701a).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA and R. Massey (California Institute of Technology)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Three-dimensional_distribution_of_dark_matter_in_the_Universe_(artist%27s_impression)_(heic0701a).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.93,
      "end": 12.65,
      "text": "In 2013, astronomers led by Istvan Horvath mapped the locations of massive stellar explosions called gamma-ray bursts.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Short Gamma-Ray Burst.jpg",
        "credit": "International Gemini Observatory/NOIRLab/NSF/AURA/J. da Silva \n\nImage processing: M. Zamani (NSF's NOIRLab)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Short_Gamma-Ray_Burst.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.933,
          "end": 7.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 7.067,
          "end": 12.633,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.65,
      "end": 19.395,
      "text": "Using NASA\u2019s Swift satellite, the team discovered a strange clustering toward the constellation Hercules.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Swift - a first-of-its-kind multi-wavelength observatory.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swift_-_a_first-of-its-kind_multi-wavelength_observatory.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.633,
          "end": 19.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.395,
      "end": 27.84,
      "text": "These bursts revealed a hidden superstructure spanning roughly ten billion light-years\u2014one-tenth of the entire observable universe.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Simulation of large scale structure (eso1438b).jpg",
        "credit": "Illustris Collaboration",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simulation_of_large_scale_structure_(eso1438b).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.4,
          "end": 23.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 23.067,
          "end": 27.833,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.84,
      "end": 33.41,
      "text": "It is so immense that it defies our core law that matter is evenly spread through space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The FLAMINGO project \u2013 cosmological hydrodynamical simulations for large-scale structure and galaxy cluster surveys.jpg",
        "credit": "Authors of the study: Schaye, Joop\u00a0; Kugel, Roi\u00a0; Schaller, Matthieu\u00a0; Helly, John C.\u00a0; Braspenning, Joey\u00a0; Elbers, Willem\u00a0; McCarthy, Ian G.\u00a0; van Daalen, Marcel P.\u00a0; Vandenbroucke, Bert\u00a0; Frenk, Car",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_FLAMINGO_project_%E2%80%93_cosmological_hydrodynamical_simulations_for_large-scale_structure_and_galaxy_cluster_surveys.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 27.833,
          "end": 31.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 31.467,
          "end": 33.4,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 33.41,
      "end": 41.435,
      "text": "This record-breaker's name was actually coined by a Filipino teenager on Wikipedia, not the discovering scientists.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Wikipedia logo Krio.png",
        "credit": "122112\u00ea",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wikipedia_logo_Krio.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 33.4,
          "end": 41.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.435,
      "end": 49.105,
      "text": "Critics argue it could be a statistical illusion, leaving the structure's true reality to be proven by future telescopes.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Wikipedia logo Krio.png",
        "credit": "122112\u00ea",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wikipedia_logo_Krio.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 41.433,
          "end": 49.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 49.105,
      "end": 55.843,
      "text": "Our best maps of the early universe suggest that a cosmic structure ten billion light-years long shouldn't exist.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Three-dimensional distribution of dark matter in the Universe (artist's impression) (heic0701a).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA and R. Massey (California Institute of Technology)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Three-dimensional_distribution_of_dark_matter_in_the_Universe_(artist%27s_impression)_(heic0701a).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 49.1,
          "end": 56.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
